>
>Talking about new ideas to Nethack, how about these:
>
Here are some more:

1) New ring: a ring of curse resistance. Wear it and when shamans,
demons, etc, point at you and curse, or when the air crackles around
them, you won't be affected. A great plus when fighting the Wiz.
Perhaps when blessed will protect you against cursed scrolls of
enchant weapon and enchant armor.

2) New amulet: an amulet of permeation. Wear it and you have that same
intrinsic that Xorns and Earth elementals have. You can walk though
walls. Again, useful for fighting tough monsters or for easily robbing
those vaults or Shopkeepers.

3) New intrinsic: stone resistance. Prevents you from turning to stone
from cockatrices, their corpses and eggs, or Medusa. Some monsters
already have this intrinsic but the player can't get it short of
polymorphing. Perhaps could combine this with a ring of stone
resistance. Eating a cockatrice or Medusa corpse should turn you to
stone, but grant the intrinsic. So if you have the ring or an extra
life-saving amulet, you could eat the corpse and then have it
permanently.

4) Make the Wizard of Yendor stone resistant so us hackers can't easily
kill him by biffing him with a cockatrice corpse.

5) Add a swimming intrinsic. Unlike water walking boots, you and your
stuff would get wet here. Could perhaps be based on exp level or
dexterity, so tough fighters without intrinsic teleportation could
fall in without getting the "you can't swim." message.

6) Bring back the scroll of destroy weapon. Makes you more weary
during enchantments and scroll identification.

7) New starting character: a (Z)ookeeper. Starts out with wimpy St and
Co, average In and Wi, and very high Dx and Ch. Starting inventory: a
bullwhip, scale mail or gloves, several taming scrolls, potions of
detect monster, maybe a spellbook of charm monster, a leash, whistle,
and several blessed figurines of various monsters so that he can start
out with more than his starting cat or dog.

8) New monsters: all a pain in the *ss like rust monsters, of course ;)
   a - A luck monster (R). When he hits you, you "feel unlucky". -1 to luck.
   b - An experience monster (R). Unlike wraiths and vampires, you fall by
       a fixed amount, say 100xp. Similar to above.
   c - A super quantum mechanic (Q). Gets a good hit on you and you're
       level teleported.
   d - A spotted dragon (D). Breaths polymorph rays. Can be a real pain
       but can be taken advantage of if you know how.
   e - Some nasty monster that can grab the weapon out of your hands and
       wield it against you. Makes you careful if you've got Mjollnir.

9) Have a potion of enlightenment tell you what your luck and
alignment are like they do when in discovery mode.

10) Post-demigod happenings. How about having a "demigod" file that
lists the players who have won and names the gods after them. i.e.
"player" wins as Neutral wizard and thereafter that altar to Thoth in
future games is called an altar to "player".

